    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Implementation and distinct reviews",
      "items": [
        "Backend: senior-golang-developer. Mobile / frontend: senior-flutter-mobile-engineer. Each owns its affected slice; a cross-stack feature uses both as needed.",
        "Architect, database, UX/UI, DevOps and SRE agents participate where their domain is affected. Agents do not all run for every change.",
        "After implementation: tests and applicable clean-code, test and docs guards; Tech Lead reviews code/security. Team Leader checks task coverage, handoffs and evidence before final gates. Findings return to the implementer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Exit and evidence",
      "items": [
        "Full applicable gates run against the final change; unavailable checks are never passing evidence.",
        "Karim manual deep review is required for auth, RBAC, deletion, Firebase Auth and upload controls. Merge requires applicable gates and required review."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Proposals from the other session",
      "items": [
        "Proposed PR evidence summary: task IDs, changed boundaries, reviewer, final revision, exact gate results, unavailable checks and risk.",
        "Required CI / protected merge checks are follow-up proposals, not verified current enforcement. F-008 can pilot with existing tasks; keep F-002 remediation separate."
      ]
    }
  ]
